        "verdict": "PASS",
        "reasons": "CONDITIONAL is justified. Price $149 (EVIDENCE), conversion 18 money-committed pre-orders / 200 unique visitors (9%) measured on this offer's own page, Brain-produced spreadsheet fulfilment (proved capability, matches the card's recorded deliverer), $4 cost, $0 exposure, 3-day settlement are all established; Brain's only missing link is MARKET_VOLUME, whose sole fact is a RECOMMENDATION ('probably'), and the plan marks it UNKNOWN rather than assuming it. Recomputed: 17 x $149 = $2,533 >= $2,500 (16 = $2,384 would fall short); ~189 more visitors at 9%; costs $68 paid from receipts, exposure 0; receipts settle day 27 inside 30. The live zero-cost forum promotion measures the channel's reachable volume in-window, with a day-7 proof and stop rules. Safe for the owner to start.",
        "findings": [
          "Validation leaves a gap: 2-4 paid orders by day 7 meets neither the proof (>=5), the stop (<2) nor continue; only the projection rule decides that band",
          "No margin: exactly 17 deals reach $2,533; a single refund or lost order misses the target, and the ledger books all 17 as one day-24 receipt",
          "Parallel low-cost research of a published studio count (Brain's parked buyerVolume question) would de-risk the volume unknown and is not scheduled"
        ],
